course: dictionary
lesson: 8781
title: Shaky: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «A shaky voice before a hospital visit means a grown-up is scared.» Here shaky means trembling, because the voice shakes from fear.
explain: Ask yourself what is shaky. Hands, legs and voices can tremble. A ladder, a shelf or a bridge can be shaky if it is not firm. A start or a spelling test can be shaky if it is not yet certain or good.
explain: «The tone of a voice — loud, quiet, shaky or flat — can show how someone feels.» Here shaky describes a voice that trembles. The word tells you how the voice sounds, so look at the thing that is shaky before you choose a meaning.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If «shaky hands» fits, the meaning is trembling. If «a shaky ladder» fits, the meaning is not firm. Check every time, because the same word can fit more than one meaning.
fact: «Shaky» means shaking or trembling, often because of fear, cold, illness or weakness.
fact: «Shaky» can also mean not firm or steady, and likely to fall or break.
fact: «Shaky» can mean not certain, strong or good, as in a shaky start.
fact: «Shakily» is the adverb. It tells you how something is done, as in moving shakily.
fact: «Shaky» is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as shaky hands or a shaky voice.
exercise: «A shaky voice before a hospital visit means a grown-up is scared.» What does shaky mean here? | Hard and firm like a rock | Very loud and proud | Strong and certain | *Trembling because of fear
exercise: A shaky ladder may fall if you climb it. What does shaky mean for a ladder? | Brand new and shiny | *
